{"data": [{"author_id": "2056484170008801280", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:22:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120296140830810455"], "id": "2120296140830810455", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 The hard part is when you need to query across those graphs and the latency kills your agent loop. We hit that wall early last year on Base.", "url": "https://x.com/petrov_base_eth/status/2120296140830810455"}, {"author_id": "2078195331557380096", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:09:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120292688499188086"], "id": "2120292688499188086", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 We solved memory and we solved it so well the big labs should be very worried.", "url": "https://x.com/kaiel_ai/status/2120292688499188086"}, {"author_id": "2107556122005540865", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:10:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120277842218901885"], "id": "2120277842218901885", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 67, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 Without a schema, can it still show which email or doc each answer came from? And what happens when a fact changes later?", "url": "https://x.com/AiXAntho/status/2120277842218901885"}, {"author_id": "1948280252", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:13:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120263637625651550"], "id": "2120263637625651550", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@anjummatin_gg @omarsar0 Yes, exactly. Thank you! Give it a try: https://t.co/O5gGzX29iY", "url": "https://x.com/graphonfounder/status/2120263637625651550"}, {"author_id": "1948280252", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:12:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120263350248784181"], "id": "2120263350248784181", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@martinOlsen94M @omarsar0 LOL, exactly.", "url": "https://x.com/graphonfounder/status/2120263350248784181"}, {"author_id": "1948280252", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:12:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120263264336785509"], "id": "2120263264336785509", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@AIGryffindor @omarsar0 Hey Kamal - we update it constantly based on new data. Give it a try: https://t.co/O5gGzX29iY", "url": "https://x.com/graphonfounder/status/2120263264336785509"}, {"author_id": "1948280252", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:41:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120255654317408759"], "id": "2120255654317408759", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kruschdev @omarsar0 @clarkzhango @deepakmishraVC @saylor feel free to reach out to us and come stop by our office", "url": "https://x.com/graphonfounder/status/2120255654317408759"}, {"author_id": "1267974208149209097", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:37:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120254469959258498"], "id": "2120254469959258498", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 @graphonfounder @clarkzhango @deepakmishraVC I'm gonna be in SF this weekend at the 8090 hackathon.  If you want to meet I'll be around.", "url": "https://x.com/kruschdev/status/2120254469959258498"}, {"author_id": "1267974208149209097", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:35:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120254116324925656"], "id": "2120254116324925656", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 Massive congrats @graphonfounder @clarkzhango @deepakmishraVC!Seeing another team converge on schema-free, bounded-context memory (&lt;8K tokens beating full-window frontier models) is awesome validation. We just finished clean-room runs across LoCoMo (90.3% / 89.7% @ 4.47K tok),", "url": "https://x.com/kruschdev/status/2120254116324925656"}, {"author_id": "15026770", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:15:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120249101304697127"], "id": "2120249101304697127", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 81, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 Whether Graphon’s approach is the answer remains to be seen, but imo the @GraphonAI team is asking exactly the right question.\n\nHow do we build a dynamic knowledge graph that evolves with the underlying data without constantly having to redesign a hand-built ontology?\n\nThere are", "url": "https://x.com/communicating/status/2120249101304697127"}, {"author_id": "1107852136086290432", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:12:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120248350188708181"], "id": "2120248350188708181", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 82, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 94% on LoCoMo at 7.9K tokens is the number I care about. Memory in my agents has mostly been stuff more context in and pray, which gets expensive fast. The schema-free graph is the interesting bit", "url": "https://x.com/anjummatin_gg/status/2120248350188708181"}, {"author_id": "1438296114260848641", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:32:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120223128974700944"], "id": "2120223128974700944", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 Memory is the thing I keep running into building an agent product. Not needing a hand-made schema is a big deal, because the schema is always where things break.", "url": "https://x.com/DylSwanepoel/status/2120223128974700944"}, {"author_id": "1165159200470650881", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:32:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120223086217981957"], "id": "2120223086217981957", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 94% on 7.9K tokens is the interesting half. LoCoMo scores have been creeping up for a while but the context budget is what decides if you can afford to run it per message. What's the cost of building the graph in the first place?", "url": "https://x.com/AIQuanting/status/2120223086217981957"}, {"author_id": "1711203486170566656", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:20:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120219952875765782"], "id": "2120219952875765782", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 69, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 94% on LoCoMo with 7.9K tokens is the interesting part, since most agent memory wins come from stuffing in more context. Schema-free graph for company data, or will it drift into mush at scale?", "url": "https://x.com/AIFlow_ML/status/2120219952875765782"}, {"author_id": "1572602236865331201", "conversation_id": "2120204152479400099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:19:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120219768976179688"], "id": "2120219768976179688", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@omarsar0 the part i'd test is when. my agent read a month old log line and swore my account was empty. it never was", "url": "https://x.com/1nspector_cat/status/2120219768976179688"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "2056484170008801280", "name": "Niko Petrov", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 66, "following_count": 87, "like_count": 3515, "listed_count": 1, "media_count": 148, "tweet_count": 1503}, "username": "petrov_base_eth"}, {"id": "2078195331557380096", "name": "Kaiel", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 24, "following_count": 29, "like_count": 6, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 13, "tweet_count": 1020}, "username": "kaiel_ai"}, {"id": "2107556122005540865", "name": "Anthony Baez", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 75, "following_count": 345, "like_count": 254, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 8, "tweet_count": 228}, "username": "AiXAntho"}, {"id": "1948280252", "name": "Arbaaz Khan", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 148, "following_count": 29, "like_count": 170, "listed_count": 2, "media_count": 10, "tweet_count": 152}, "username": "graphonfounder"}, {"id": "1267974208149209097", "name": "Saylor", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 223, "following_count": 378, "like_count": 1988, "listed_count": 2, "media_count": 178, "tweet_count": 2851}, "username": "kruschdev"}, {"id": "15026770", "name": "Christopher", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 2076, "following_count": 246, "like_count": 32461, "listed_count": 225, "media_count": 59, "tweet_count": 27165}, "username": "communicating"}, {"id": "1107852136086290432", "name": "Anjum Matin | AI Engi